                <pb facs="d135-2" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v07-09mSupp/d135-2"/>

                <head>136. Memorandum for the Record Prepared by McCone, July 27<anchor n="1" xml:id="d136-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1962-07-27">July 27, 1962</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d136-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d136-1"/>
                <p>Dr. Edward Teller called at my home at 1:30 on July 27th; expressed concern over
                    the possibility that we were going to enter a moratorium of a test suspension
                    without reasonable means of verification.</p>
                <p>I discussed at some length the two risks, one being the loss of our nuclear
                    superiority if we stopped and Russia proceeded clandestinely; the other being
                    the dangers inherent in nuclear proliferation. I told Dr. Teller that there was
                    no danger of our entering an agreement which <pb facs="0519" n="368"
                        type="typeset" xml:id="pg368"/> would suspend all testing unless reasonable
                    means of verification were agreed upon.</p>
                <p>Dr. Teller then spoke of the enormous developments possible as a result of the
                    breakthrough in the [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]
                    experiment. I told Dr. Teller I did not feel that the true significance of this
                    breakthrough was understood and that he should be sure Seaborg and Dr. Harold Brown fully appreciated this fact and brought it to the
                    attention of their superiors and to the President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_MJA_1">John A.
                            McCone
                    </signed><affiliation>Director</affiliation>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d136-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d136-f1-content">
                <p>Meeting with Dr. Teller regarding verification issue. Secret. 1 p. CIA Files, Job 80B01285A, DCI Memos for the Record, 4/7/62–8/21/62.</p>
            </note>
